---
import '@fontsource/sora/400.css';
import '@fontsource/sora/600.css';
import '../../styles/emd-finder.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"/><title>EMD Finder | NC Digital Admin</title></head>
<body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/admin/links/">NC <span>Digital</span><small>/ EMD Finder</small></a><nav><a href="/admin/keyword-research/">Keyword research</a><a href="/admin/links/">All tools ↗</a></nav></header>
<main>
  <div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">SOUTH WALES · LOCAL LEAD GENERATION</p><h1>Find the overlooked.<br/><span>Check the opportunity.</span></h1><p>Available domain ideas, real search demand and the businesses you would need to outrank.</p></div><div class="budget-badge"><strong>$1</strong><span>maximum per scan<br/>browse saved data free</span></div></div>
  <section class="panel" aria-label="Find opportunities"><form id="finder-form"><div class="form-grid">
    <label>Discovery mode<select id="mode"><option value="balanced">Balanced · 50+ searches / £500+ job</option><option value="value">High value · 20+ searches / £1,500+ job</option><option value="explore">Explore · unreported search volume</option></select></label>
    <label>Service<input id="service" list="services" placeholder="All services, or type a new one" maxlength="70"/><datalist id="services"></datalist></label>
    <label>Town<input id="town" list="towns" placeholder="All South Wales towns" maxlength="70"/><datalist id="towns"></datalist></label>
    <label>Scan budget (USD)<input id="budget" type="number" value="1" min="0.05" max="1" step="0.01" required/></label>
  </div><details class="advanced"><summary>New service / job value assumption</summary><label>Estimated value of one completed job (£)<input id="job-value" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" placeholder="Use existing editable estimates"/></label><p>For a new idea, enter both a service and a town. The job value override applies to this selection. This is your assumption, not DataForSEO data.</p></details>
  <div class="form-footer"><p id="preview">Loading your existing research…</p><button type="submit" class="primary" id="scan-button" disabled>Find opportunities ↗</button></div></form></section>
  <div id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
  <section id="scan-progress" class="panel progress" hidden><div><p class="eyebrow">SCAN PROGRESS</p><h2 id="phase"></h2><p id="spend"></p><p id="scan-warnings"></p></div><div class="actions"><button id="resume" hidden>Resume scan</button><button id="stop">Stop scan</button></div></section>
  <div class="summary"><div><strong id="total">—</strong><span>matching ideas</span></div><div><strong id="available">—</strong><span>recently unregistered</span></div><div><strong id="promising">—</strong><span>promising link evidence</span></div><div><strong id="saved-count">—</strong><span>on your watchlist</span></div></div>
  <section aria-label="Opportunities"><div class="results-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR OPPORTUNITIES</p><h2>Shortlist before you spend.</h2></div><button id="export">Export CSV</button></div>
  <div class="filters"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Filter these results…" aria-label="Filter results"/><select id="view" aria-label="Opportunity status"><option value="active">Active ideas</option><option value="watchlist">Watchlist</option><option value="purchased">Purchased</option><option value="partner-found">Partner found</option><option value="dismissed">Dismissed</option><option value="all">All statuses</option></select><select id="sort" aria-label="Sort results"><option value="priority">Sort: opportunity</option><option value="volume">Sort: search volume</option><option value="jobValue">Sort: job value</option></select><select id="saved-scan" aria-label="Saved scan"><option value="">All research / saved scans…</option></select></div>
  <p class="hint">Searches are monthly UK estimates for the exact phrase. Job values are editable assumptions. “Unverified” means more evidence is needed.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Domain / target keyword</th><th>UK searches / mo</th><th>Job value / commission</th><th>Organic competition</th><th>Registration check</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div>
  <button id="more" hidden>Show 50 more</button><p id="empty" class="empty" hidden>No ideas match these filters. Try another mode or service.</p>
  </section>
  <details class="panel methodology"><summary>How the finder spends less & how to read the evidence</summary><p>Existing research is loaded first. A scan considers up to 100 phrases, checks up to 30 domains, investigates up to 20 available domains in local Google results, and runs one bulk link check for up to five finalists. Repeated scans reuse keyword metrics for 90 days, local results for 30 days, link counts for 90 days and registration checks for one day.</p><p>Keyword metrics come from DataForSEO Google UK data. Organic difficulty and paid CPC are different measurements; CPC is not job value or commission. Link evidence compares the median referring domains of non-directory competitors, with ranking-page link counts shown separately. Fewer than five organic results or incomplete link data stays Unverified. A median below 15 is labelled Promising, 15–29 Moderate and 30+ Defended. These are screening heuristics, not ranking predictions.</p><p>Directory-heavy results can signal an opening, but also strong competitors. Google Maps can take clicks. Check the actual results, service fit and a willing local partner before deciding. Similar phrases share demand, so volumes are not added together. An exact-match domain does not guarantee a ranking advantage.</p><p>July research retains its original date. Old availability is not current availability. A Nominet RDAP 404 means the domain appears unregistered; reserved names or registrar restrictions can still prevent purchase. Recheck with a registrar before buying.</p><p>Estimates are in USD and use standard endpoint rates with conservative spending reservations. The server stops dispatching requests when the next reservation would exceed your budget. Failed or interrupted requests keep their reservation counted because they may have been charged. They are not automatically retried. No domain is purchased by this tool.</p><p><a href="https://docs.dataforseo.com/v3/backlinks/bulk_referring_domains/live/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DataForSEO link metrics ↗</a> · <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ranking-systems-guide#exact-match-domain" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google on exact-match domains ↗</a></p></details>
</main>
<dialog id="detail"><div class="dialog-header"><p class="eyebrow">OPPORTUNITY NOTES</p><button id="close-detail" aria-label="Close details">✕</button></div><div id="detail-content"></div></dialog>
<script>import '../../scripts/emd-finder.js';</script>
</body></html>
